sequenceDiagram
  participant Lead as Program Lead (browser)
  participant Shell as Shell/CyberRoutes
  participant Scope as CyberScopeContext
  participant Portfolio as CyberPortfolio screen
  participant Data as cyberData/selectors (fixtures)
  participant MemberHome as CyberMemberScreens

  Lead->>Shell: navigate to /cyber/portfolio
  Shell->>Scope: useCyberScope() read role
  Scope-->>Shell: role = Program Lead
  Shell->>Portfolio: render CyberPortfolio
  Portfolio->>Data: load cyberMembers, cyberTiers, cyberFindings, cyberIncidents (all facilities)
  Data-->>Portfolio: full portfolio rows
  Portfolio->>Portfolio: compute KPI strip (enrolled, avg grade, open P1/P2, SLA met %, remediation %)
  Portfolio-->>Lead: render KPI strip, grade distribution, tier mix, AI summary (static, labelled illustrative)
  Lead->>Portfolio: set facility type / province filter
  Portfolio->>Data: recompute distribution + tier mix + median benchmark over filtered subset
  Data-->>Portfolio: filtered aggregates + facility-type median
  Portfolio-->>Lead: updated chart and benchmark panel
  Portfolio->>Portfolio: rank members by attention score (open P1, grade drop, overdue criticals, silent sources)
  Portfolio-->>Lead: render attention list with one-line reasons
  Portfolio-->>Lead: render province grouping with grade colour indicator
  Lead->>Portfolio: click member row
  Portfolio->>Scope: set viewAs(memberId, readOnly=true)
  Scope-->>Portfolio: ack
  Portfolio->>Shell: navigate(/cyber/members/:id)
  Shell->>MemberHome: render member home
  MemberHome->>Scope: useCyberScope() read readOnly flag
  Scope-->>MemberHome: readOnly = true
  MemberHome-->>Lead: render member home with illustrative banner, mutating actions disabled
